.TH AVR\-AUTH\-STATUS 1 "" "avr 0.1.2" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-auth-status \- Display the authenticated user and connection state.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr auth status
[OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Display the authenticated user and connection state.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-show\-token\fR
Display the auth token in plain text.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR \fITEXT\fR
Output JSON. Pass comma-separated field names, "*" for all fields, or "?" to list available fields.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-jq\fR \fITEXT\fR
Filter --json output through a jq expression.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-auth (1),
.BR avr-auth-login (1),
.BR avr-auth-logout (1),
.BR avr-auth-switch (1)
